(function(E){ const x = E["exam-02"] = E["exam-02"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x02-l3"] = {"id":"x02-l3","patterns":["L3-science","PARA-opinion"],"title":{"en":"Listening Part 3: a tutorial and a plan","tr":"Listening Part 3: bir görüşme ve bir plan","fa":"Listening Part 3: یک جلسه با استاد و یک برنامه"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to follow a three-person tutorial: pick out what the tutor praises and criticises, tell a worry from a decision, and complete a flow-chart of next steps from a box.","tr":"Bu derste üç kişilik bir görüşmeyi takip etmeyi öğreneceksin: öğretim görevlisinin neyi övdüğünü ve eleştirdiğini bulacak, bir endişeyi bir karardan ayıracak ve bir kutudan seçerek sonraki adımların akış şemasını tamamlayacaksın.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یک جلسه‌ی سه‌نفره با استاد را دنبال کنی: چیزهایی را که استاد تعریف یا نقد می‌کند پیدا کنی، نگرانی را از تصمیم جدا کنی و فلوچارتِ قدم‌های بعدی را از روی یک کادر کامل کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Listening Part 3: a tutorial and a plan","tr":"Listening Part 3: bir görüşme ve bir plan","fa":"Listening Part 3: یک جلسه با استاد و یک برنامه"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to follow a three-person tutorial: pick out what the tutor praises and criticises, tell a worry from a decision, and complete a flow-chart of next steps from a box.","tr":"Bu derste üç kişilik bir görüşmeyi takip etmeyi öğreneceksin: öğretim görevlisinin neyi övdüğünü ve eleştirdiğini bulacak, bir endişeyi bir karardan ayıracak ve bir kutudan seçerek sonraki adımların akış şemasını tamamlayacaksın.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یک جلسه‌ی سه‌نفره با استاد را دنبال کنی: چیزهایی را که استاد تعریف یا نقد می‌کند پیدا کنی، نگرانی را از تصمیم جدا کنی و فلوچارتِ قدم‌های بعدی را از روی یک کادر کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"10"},{"label":{"en":"Speakers","tr":"Konuşan","fa":"گوینده"},"value":"3"},{"label":{"en":"Box","tr":"Kutu","fa":"کادر"},"value":"A-F"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: feedback on a nutrition project","tr":"Bu sınav: bir beslenme projesine geri bildirim","fa":"این آزمون: بازخورد درباره‌ی یک پروژه‌ی تغذیه"},"intro":{"en":"Part 3 is students talking about their studies, often with a tutor. Science projects are one of the two most frequent situations. The questions follow the conversation: opinions first, then a plan.","tr":"Part 3, öğrencilerin dersleri hakkında, çoğu zaman bir öğretim görevlisiyle yaptığı konuşmadır. Bilim projeleri en sık çıkan iki durumdan biridir. Sorular konuşmayı izler: önce görüşler, sonra bir plan.","fa":"Part 3 گفتگوی دانشجوهاست درباره‌ی درسشان، اغلب همراه یک استاد. پروژه‌های علمی یکی از دو موقعیت پرتکرارند. سؤال‌ها دنبال گفتگو می‌آیند: اول نظرها، بعد یک برنامه."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x02-l3-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["L3-science","PARA-opinion"],"often":{"pattern":"L3-science","n":19,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Feedback on a science project","tr":"Bir bilim projesine geri bildirim","fa":"بازخورد درباره‌ی یک پروژه‌ی علمی"},"asks":{"en":"A tutor gives two students feedback on a food-science experiment: what was good, what must be fixed and which parts of the course helped. Then they plan the changes in order, shown as a flow-chart.","tr":"Bir öğretim görevlisi iki öğrenciye bir gıda bilimi deneyi hakkında geri bildirim veriyor: neyin iyi olduğu, neyin düzeltilmesi gerektiği ve dersin hangi bölümlerinin yardımcı olduğu. Sonra değişiklikleri sırayla planlıyorlar; bu bir akış şemasında gösteriliyor.","fa":"یک استاد به دو دانشجو درباره‌ی یک آزمایش علوم غذایی بازخورد می‌دهد: چه چیزی خوب بود، چه چیزی باید درست شود و کدام بخش‌های درس کمک کرد. بعد تغییرها را به ترتیب برنامه‌ریزی می‌کنند که در یک فلوچارت نشان داده می‌شود."},"fields":["What the tutor liked","What must be fixed","Useful parts of the course","The plan: first","The plan: next","The plan: last"],"words":[{"a":"praise","b":"there’s a lot to like / that was excellent","tr":"övmek","fa":"تعریف کردن"},{"a":"a strength","b":"what worked well","tr":"güçlü yön","fa":"نقطه‌ی قوت"},{"a":"sample size","b":"how many portions or people you tested","tr":"örneklem büyüklüğü","fa":"حجم نمونه"},{"a":"limited","b":"not enough / only a few","tr":"sınırlı","fa":"محدود"},{"a":"unreliable source","b":"a site that wants to sell you something","tr":"güvenilmez kaynak","fa":"منبع غیرقابل‌اعتماد"},{"a":"within the word limit","b":"not too long","tr":"kelime sınırı içinde","fa":"داخل سقف کلمه"},{"a":"revise","b":"make changes / a new version","tr":"gözden geçirip düzeltmek","fa":"بازنگری کردن"},{"a":"repetitive","b":"the same thing again and again","tr":"tekrarlayıcı","fa":"تکراری"},{"a":"useful","b":"it really helped / I finally understood","tr":"faydalı","fa":"مفید"},{"a":"not necessary","b":"I don’t think we need to","tr":"gerekli değil","fa":"لازم نیست"},{"a":"replace X with Y","b":"use Y instead of X","tr":"X yerine Y kullanmak","fa":"به جای X از Y استفاده کردن"},{"a":"first","b":"that has to come first / before anything else","tr":"önce","fa":"اول"}],"traps":[{"en":"A student’s worry is not the tutor’s view: \"I thought you’d say it was too long.\" \"No, it’s fine.\" Wait for the tutor’s answer.","tr":"Öğrencinin endişesi öğretim görevlisinin görüşü değildir: \"Çok uzun diyeceğinizi düşünmüştüm.\" \"Hayır, iyi.\" Görevlinin cevabını bekle.","fa":"نگرانیِ دانشجو نظر استاد نیست: «فکر کردم می‌گویید خیلی طولانی است». «نه، خوب است». منتظر جواب استاد بمان."},{"en":"A step suggested and then dropped: \"Should we ask a technician?\" \"I don’t think that’s necessary.\" It is in the box, but it is not in the plan.","tr":"Önerilip sonra bırakılan bir adım: \"Bir teknisyene soralım mı?\" \"Bence gerekli değil.\" Kutuda var ama planda yok.","fa":"قدمی که پیشنهاد و بعد کنار گذاشته می‌شود: «از یک تکنسین بپرسیم؟» «فکر نمی‌کنم لازم باشد». در کادر هست، اما در برنامه نیست."}],"example":{"lines":[["Tutor","Your interviews were very useful. The questionnaire was less successful: too many questions were unclear."],["Student","So should we drop it?"],["Tutor","No, just rewrite the unclear questions."]],"item":"What does the tutor think about the questionnaire? A It was a strength. B It needs some changes. C It should be removed.","answer":"B","why":{"en":"It was \"less successful\", but the tutor says \"no\" to dropping it: rewrite the unclear questions.","tr":"\"Daha az başarılı\" ama görevli onu çıkarmaya \"hayır\" diyor: belirsiz soruları yeniden yaz.","fa":"«کمتر موفق» بود، اما استاد به حذفش «نه» می‌گوید: سؤال‌های نامفهوم را دوباره بنویسید."}}},{"id":"L3-science","ctx":["L3-science"],"title":{"en":"Nature, environment and experiments","tr":"Doğa, çevre ve deneyler","fa":"طبیعت، محیط زیست و آزمایش"},"asks":{"en":"Two students, sometimes with a tutor, plan or review a project on an experiment, an animal or plant, the sea, a volcano or recycling. Questions ask what they decide, what they think of a source or a method, what went wrong and what they will do next.","tr":"İki öğrenci, bazen bir hocayla, bir deney, bir hayvan ya da bitki, deniz, bir yanardağ ya da geri dönüşüm üzerine bir projeyi planlar ya da değerlendirir. Sorular neye karar verdiklerini, bir kaynak ya da yöntem hakkında ne düşündüklerini, neyin ters gittiğini ve sırada ne yapacaklarını sorar.","fa":"دو دانشجو، گاهی با یک استاد، پروژه‌ای درباره‌ی یک آزمایش، یک حیوان یا گیاه، دریا، یک آتشفشان یا بازیافت را برنامه‌ریزی یا بررسی می‌کنند. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند به چه تصمیمی می‌رسند، درباره‌ی یک منبع یا روش چه فکر می‌کنند، چه چیزی خراب شد و قدم بعدی‌شان چیست."},"fields":["What was the aim of the experiment?","What went wrong with the first method?","What do they decide to change?","Which TWO findings surprised them?","Complete the flow-chart of the procedure."],"words":[{"a":"experiment","b":"the test we ran","tr":"deney","fa":"آزمایش"},{"a":"hypothesis","b":"what we expected to find","tr":"hipotez","fa":"فرضیه"},{"a":"sample","b":"the seeds we tested / the group","tr":"örneklem","fa":"نمونه"},{"a":"variable","b":"the thing we changed","tr":"değişken","fa":"متغیر"},{"a":"results","b":"what we found","tr":"sonuçlar","fa":"نتیجه‌ها"},{"a":"unexpected","b":"we didn't predict that","tr":"beklenmedik","fa":"غیرمنتظره"},{"a":"reliable","b":"we can trust it","tr":"güvenilir","fa":"قابل اعتماد"},{"a":"measure","b":"record how much or how tall","tr":"ölçmek","fa":"اندازه گرفتن"},{"a":"species","b":"kinds of animal or plant","tr":"tür","fa":"گونه"},{"a":"extinct","b":"died out / no longer exists","tr":"soyu tükenmiş","fa":"منقرض"},{"a":"sustainable","b":"doesn't harm the planet","tr":"sürdürülebilir","fa":"پایدار"},{"a":"recycle","b":"use the material again","tr":"geri dönüştürmek","fa":"بازیافت کردن"},{"a":"procedure","b":"the steps we followed","tr":"işlem sırası","fa":"روش کار"}],"traps":[{"en":"Flow-charts: steps are not always said in time order (\"before that, we soaked them\"). Put them in the order they happened.","tr":"Akış şemaları: adımlar her zaman zaman sırasıyla söylenmez (\"ondan önce onları ıslattık\"). Onları olduğu sıraya koy.","fa":"فلوچارت‌ها: مرحله‌ها همیشه به ترتیب زمانی گفته نمی‌شوند («قبلش خیسشان کردیم»). به ترتیبی که اتفاق افتادند بچینشان."},{"en":"Result against expectation: \"we thought light would matter most, but actually temperature did\".","tr":"Beklentiye karşı sonuç: \"ışığın en önemli olduğunu sanıyorduk ama aslında sıcaklıkmış\".","fa":"نتیجه در برابر انتظار: «فکر می‌کردیم نور از همه مهم‌تر است، ولی در واقع دما بود»."}],"example":{"lines":[["Tutor","What affected germination most?"],["Student","We expected light to make the biggest difference."],["Student","But in fact the seeds we kept warm grew fastest, whatever the light."]],"item":"Which factor had the greatest effect?  A light   B temperature   C water","answer":"B","why":{"en":"Light was the expectation. \"In fact\" introduces the result: the warm seeds grew fastest, so temperature.","tr":"Işık beklentiydi. \"In fact\" sonucu getiriyor: sıcak tutulan tohumlar en hızlı büyüdü, yani sıcaklık.","fa":"نور انتظارشان بود. «In fact» نتیجه را می‌آورد: دانه‌های گرم سریع‌تر رشد کردند، پس دما."}},"general":true,"patterns":["L3-science"],"often":{"pattern":"L3-science","n":19,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}},{"id":"L3-food","ctx":["L3-food","L3-science"],"title":{"en":"Food, health and the mind","tr":"Beslenme, sağlık ve zihin","fa":"غذا، سلامت و ذهن"},"asks":{"en":"Two students, sometimes with a tutor, plan or review a project on food, diet, sleep or how people think and feel. Questions ask what they decide, what they think of a source or a method, what went wrong and what they will do next.","tr":"İki öğrenci, bazen bir hocayla, yiyecek, beslenme, uyku ya da insanların nasıl düşünüp hissettiği üzerine bir projeyi planlar ya da değerlendirir. Sorular neye karar verdiklerini, bir kaynak ya da yöntem hakkında ne düşündüklerini, neyin ters gittiğini ve sırada ne yapacaklarını sorar.","fa":"دو دانشجو، گاهی با یک استاد، پروژه‌ای درباره‌ی غذا، رژیم غذایی، خواب یا اینکه آدم‌ها چطور فکر می‌کنند و چه حسی دارند را برنامه‌ریزی یا بررسی می‌کنند. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند به چه تصمیمی می‌رسند، درباره‌ی یک منبع یا روش چه فکر می‌کنند، چه چیزی خراب شد و قدم بعدی‌شان چیست."},"fields":["What did the survey show about eating habits?","What is the students’ opinion of the article?","Which TWO factors are linked to poor sleep?","What does each study suggest?"],"words":[{"a":"diet","b":"what people eat","tr":"beslenme","fa":"رژیم غذایی"},{"a":"nutrition","b":"the goodness in food","tr":"besin değeri","fa":"تغذیه"},{"a":"ingredients","b":"what it's made from","tr":"içindekiler","fa":"مواد تشکیل‌دهنده"},{"a":"label","b":"the information on the packet","tr":"etiket","fa":"برچسب"},{"a":"obesity","b":"being seriously overweight","tr":"obezite","fa":"چاقی"},{"a":"consumers","b":"the people who buy it","tr":"tüketiciler","fa":"مصرف‌کننده‌ها"},{"a":"participants","b":"the people in the study","tr":"katılımcılar","fa":"شرکت‌کننده‌ها"},{"a":"linked to","b":"is connected with","tr":"... ile bağlantılı","fa":"مرتبط با"},{"a":"anxiety","b":"worry / feeling stressed","tr":"kaygı","fa":"اضطراب"},{"a":"lifestyle","b":"the way people live","tr":"yaşam tarzı","fa":"سبک زندگی"},{"a":"evidence","b":"data that shows it","tr":"kanıt","fa":"شواهد"},{"a":"misleading","b":"gives the wrong idea","tr":"yanıltıcı","fa":"گمراه‌کننده"},{"a":"sample size","b":"how many people were tested","tr":"örneklem büyüklüğü","fa":"حجم نمونه"}],"traps":[{"en":"The study’s claim and the students’ view are different: \"the article says sugar is the main cause, but I think that’s too simple\".","tr":"Çalışmanın iddiası ile öğrencilerin görüşü farklıdır: \"makale asıl nedenin şeker olduğunu söylüyor ama bence bu fazla basit\".","fa":"ادعای پژوهش با نظر دانشجوها فرق دارد: «مقاله می‌گوید علت اصلی شکر است، ولی به نظرم این خیلی ساده‌انگارانه است»."},{"en":"Survey numbers: \"most people\", \"a few people\" and \"nobody\" lead to different answers.","tr":"Anket sayıları: \"çoğu insan\", \"birkaç kişi\" ve \"hiç kimse\" farklı cevaplara götürür.","fa":"عددهای نظرسنجی: «بیشتر آدم‌ها»، «چند نفر» و «هیچ‌کس» به جواب‌های متفاوت می‌رسند."}],"example":{"lines":[["Student A","The article blames phones for poor sleep."],["Student B","Partly, but the study we read found that late coffee was a bigger factor."],["Student A","True. The data on caffeine was much stronger."]],"item":"What do the students agree is the main factor?  A mobile phones   B late caffeine   C noise","answer":"B","why":{"en":"Phones are only \"partly\" to blame. Both students accept that the caffeine data was stronger.","tr":"Telefonlar yalnızca \"kısmen\" suçlu. İki öğrenci de kafein verisinin daha güçlü olduğunu kabul ediyor.","fa":"گوشی فقط «تا حدی» مقصر است. هر دو دانشجو قبول می‌کنند که داده‌های کافئین قوی‌تر بود."}},"general":true,"patterns":["L3-science"],"often":{"pattern":"L3-science","n":19,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Three pairs, then a flow-chart","tr":"Üç çift soru, sonra bir akış şeması","fa":"سه جفت سؤال، بعد یک فلوچارت"},"body":{"en":"Questions 21-26 are three choose-TWO questions. After a short break, Questions 27-30 are a flow-chart: choose FOUR answers from a box of six, A-F, each letter once. Three people speak, so note who says what.","tr":"Soru 21-26 üç tane iki-seçenekli sorudur. Kısa bir aradan sonra Soru 27-30 bir akış şemasıdır: A-F arasındaki altı seçenekten DÖRT cevap seç, her harf bir kez. Üç kişi konuşuyor; kimin ne dediğini not et.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۲۱ تا ۲۶ سه سؤالِ «دو گزینه» هستند. بعد از یک مکث کوتاه، سؤال‌های ۲۷ تا ۳۰ یک فلوچارت‌اند: از کادر شش‌تایی A تا F چهار جواب انتخاب کن، هر حرف یک بار. سه نفر حرف می‌زنند، پس یادداشت کن چه کسی چه می‌گوید."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Follow the order words","tr":"Sıra bildiren kelimeleri izle","fa":"کلمه‌های ترتیب را دنبال کن"},"steps":[{"en":"Before you listen, read the box and give each option a short label in your head.","tr":"Dinlemeden önce kutuyu oku ve her seçeneğe aklında kısa bir ad ver.","fa":"قبل از گوش دادن کادر را بخوان و در ذهنت به هر گزینه یک اسم کوتاه بده."},{"en":"Listen for the order: first, then, once you have, after that, the last step.","tr":"Sırayı dinle: first, then, once you have, after that, the last step.","fa":"به ترتیب گوش بده: first، then، once you have، after that، the last step."},{"en":"A step counts only when the speakers agree to it. Cross out what they turn down.","tr":"Bir adım ancak konuşanlar onu kabul ederse geçerlidir. Reddettiklerinin üstünü çiz.","fa":"یک قدم فقط وقتی حساب است که گوینده‌ها قبولش کنند. چیزهایی را که رد می‌کنند خط بزن."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Who decides?","tr":"Kim karar veriyor?","fa":"چه کسی تصمیم می‌گیرد؟"},"body":{"en":"In a tutorial the tutor usually has the final word. A student may suggest or fear something; the answer is what the tutor accepts. Listen for \"No, that’s fine\", \"I don’t think that’s necessary\" and \"Fair enough\".","tr":"Bir görüşmede son sözü genelde öğretim görevlisi söyler. Öğrenci bir şey önerebilir ya da bir şeyden korkabilir; cevap, görevlinin kabul ettiği şeydir. \"No, that’s fine\", \"I don’t think that’s necessary\" ve \"Fair enough\" ifadelerine kulak ver.","fa":"در جلسه با استاد، معمولاً حرف آخر را استاد می‌زند. دانشجو ممکن است چیزی پیشنهاد کند یا از چیزی بترسد؛ جواب چیزی است که استاد قبول می‌کند. به «No, that’s fine»، «I don’t think that’s necessary» و «Fair enough» گوش بده."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One flow-chart step, step by step","tr":"Bir akış şeması adımı, adım adım","fa":"یک مرحله‌ی فلوچارت، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the flow-chart. Choose the correct letter from the box: A collect new data  B use the survey data  C interview farmers","item":"Step 2: ___","lines":[["Student","After the reading, should we interview some farmers?"],["Tutor","That would take months. Use the survey data you already have."],["Student","OK, so next we use the survey data."]],"answer":"B","walk":[{"en":"The step comes after the reading, so listen for \"after\" and \"next\".","tr":"Adım okumadan sonra geliyor; \"after\" ve \"next\" kelimelerine kulak ver.","fa":"این قدم بعد از مطالعه است، پس به «after» و «next» گوش بده."},{"en":"Interviews are suggested, but the tutor turns them down: \"That would take months.\"","tr":"Röportajlar öneriliyor ama görevli reddediyor: \"Aylar sürer.\"","fa":"مصاحبه پیشنهاد می‌شود، اما استاد ردش می‌کند: «ماه‌ها طول می‌کشد»."},{"en":"The student confirms the next step: use the survey data. Write B.","tr":"Öğrenci sonraki adımı doğruluyor: anket verilerini kullanmak. B yaz.","fa":"دانشجو قدم بعدی را تأیید می‌کند: استفاده از داده‌های نظرسنجی. B را بنویس."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Student: \"I was worried our charts were too small.\" Tutor: \"No, they’re fine. The problem is the missing labels.\" What does the tutor want changed?","options":["the labels","the size of the charts","nothing"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The size was the student’s worry; the tutor says \"No, they’re fine\". The problem is the missing labels.","tr":"Boyut öğrencinin endişesiydi; görevli \"Hayır, iyiler\" diyor. Sorun eksik etiketler.","fa":"اندازه نگرانیِ دانشجو بود؛ استاد می‌گوید «نه، خوب‌اند». مشکل برچسب‌های جاافتاده است."}},"remember":{"en":"In a tutorial, the answer is what the tutor accepts. In a flow-chart, follow the order words and cross out rejected steps.","tr":"Bir görüşmede cevap, görevlinin kabul ettiği şeydir. Akış şemasında sıra kelimelerini izle ve reddedilen adımları çiz.","fa":"در جلسه با استاد، جواب چیزی است که استاد قبول می‌کند. در فلوچارت، کلمه‌های ترتیب را دنبال کن و قدم‌های ردشده را خط بزن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x02-l3-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-l3"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"listening","part":"Listening Part 3","title":{"en":"Feedback on a nutrition project","tr":"Bir beslenme projesine geri bildirim","fa":"بازخورد درباره‌ی یک پروژه‌ی تغذیه"},"timed":7,"ctx":["L3-science"],"script":[{"who":"Tutor","line":"Come in, both of you. So, I've read your project on cooking methods and vitamin C in broccoli, and I wanted to give you some feedback before you revise it."},{"who":"Maya","line":"Thanks. We were quite nervous about it, to be honest."},{"who":"Tutor","line":"Well, there's a lot to like. Your description of the method was very clear. Anyone could repeat your experiment from what you've written, and that's exactly what a method section should do."},{"who":"Dev","line":"That's good to hear. We spent ages on that part."},{"who":"Tutor","line":"And the way you presented the results was excellent. The charts were very easy to read, and you chose the right type of chart for each comparison. Now, the sample size: you only tested three portions for each cooking method, which is rather small, so I wouldn't call that a strength. And the literature review was limited, I'm afraid. Most of it came from just two or three textbooks."},{"who":"Maya","line":"We did wonder about that. What about the conclusion?"},{"who":"Tutor","line":"The conclusion goes a little further than your data allows. We'll come back to that. First, the problems I'd like you to fix."},{"who":"Dev","line":"I thought you might say the title was too long. It's nearly two lines."},{"who":"Tutor","line":"No, the title's fine. It says exactly what you did. The first real problem is with two of your sources. They're commercial websites that sell vitamin supplements, so they can't be treated as neutral. You need to take them out."},{"who":"Maya","line":"Oh. We didn't notice who ran those sites."},{"who":"Tutor","line":"It's an easy mistake. The second problem is more serious. You bought the broccoli on different days and from different shops, so the vitamin C levels may have been different before you even started cooking."},{"who":"Dev","line":"That's true. Some of it looked much fresher than the rest."},{"who":"Maya","line":"Is the report too long? I was worried we'd gone over the word limit."},{"who":"Tutor","line":"Not at all, you're well within it. And you recorded the cooking temperatures carefully, which many groups forget. Now, before we plan the changes, tell me how you found the course as a whole. Which parts helped you most with this project?"},{"who":"Maya","line":"For me, the statistics workshop. I'd always been scared of statistics, but after that session I finally understood how to compare our results properly."},{"who":"Dev","line":"I agree, that workshop was really useful. The lab safety sessions were fine, but they were a bit repetitive. For me, the best thing was the guest talk by the food scientist. Hearing how a real company tests its products gave us the idea for this project."},{"who":"Maya","line":"It's a pity the farm visit was cancelled because of the weather. That might have been good too."},{"who":"Dev","line":"And there were the online quizzes, but to be honest I didn't bother with those much."},{"who":"Tutor","line":"That's helpful, thank you. Right, let's plan the revision step by step. What's the first thing you need to do?"},{"who":"Maya","line":"Sort out the broccoli problem, I suppose. So this time we buy all the vegetables from a single supplier, and on the same day."},{"who":"Tutor","line":"Yes, that has to come first, because everything else depends on it. Then what?"},{"who":"Dev","line":"Should we ask a technician to check the equipment? Maybe the scales were wrong."},{"who":"Tutor","line":"I don't think that's necessary. The equipment was checked at the start of term. What I would like is more tests."},{"who":"Dev","line":"So the next step is to increase the number of tests. Five portions for each method instead of three?"},{"who":"Tutor","line":"Five would be much better. Once you have the new results, you'll analyse them again with the method from the statistics workshop."},{"who":"Maya","line":"And after that we fix the sources. We'll use journal articles instead of the websites."},{"who":"Tutor","line":"Good. The library can show you how to search the journals. And should you add photographs of the samples? Some groups do."},{"who":"Dev","line":"I don't think photos would add much. Everyone knows what broccoli looks like."},{"who":"Tutor","line":"Fair enough. So the last step is the one we talked about earlier."},{"who":"Maya","line":"The conclusion. We'll rewrite it so that it only says what the new data actually shows."},{"who":"Tutor","line":"Exactly. Send me the new version in three weeks, and we'll meet again after that."}],"groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 21-22. Choose TWO letters, A-E.","qtype":"mcq2","questions":[{"n":21,"n2":22,"kind":"mcq2","prompt":"Which TWO things does the tutor praise in the students’ project?","options":["A the number of portions tested","B how well the procedure was explained","C the range of sources in the literature review","D the charts used for the results","E the conclusion"],"correct":[1,3],"evidence":"Your description of the method was very clear","why":{"en":"B \"Your description of the method was very clear\" and D \"The charts were very easy to read\". The sample was \"rather small\", the literature review \"limited\", and the conclusion goes too far.","tr":"B \"Yöntem tanımınız çok açıktı\" ve D \"Grafikler çok kolay okunuyordu\". Örneklem \"oldukça küçük\", kaynak taraması \"sınırlı\", sonuç da fazla ileri gidiyor.","fa":"B «توضیح روشِ کارتان خیلی روشن بود» و D «نمودارها خیلی راحت خوانده می‌شدند». نمونه «نسبتاً کوچک» بود، مرور منابع «محدود» و نتیجه‌گیری بیش از حد جلو رفته."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 23-24. Choose TWO letters, A-E.","qtype":"mcq2","questions":[{"n":23,"n2":24,"kind":"mcq2","prompt":"Which TWO problems does the tutor say the students must fix?","options":["A The title is too long.","B Some sources are not neutral.","C The report is over the word limit.","D The broccoli was not all bought at the same time and place.","E The cooking temperatures were not recorded."],"correct":[1,3],"evidence":"They're commercial websites that sell vitamin supplements","why":{"en":"B: two sources are websites that sell supplements, so they are not neutral. D: the broccoli came from different shops on different days. The title is \"fine\", the report is \"well within\" the limit, and the temperatures were recorded.","tr":"B: iki kaynak takviye satan siteler, yani tarafsız değiller. D: brokoli farklı günlerde farklı dükkânlardan alınmış. Başlık \"iyi\", rapor sınırın \"epey altında\" ve sıcaklıklar kaydedilmiş.","fa":"B: دو منبع سایت‌هایی‌اند که مکمل می‌فروشند، پس بی‌طرف نیستند. D: بروکلی در روزهای مختلف از مغازه‌های مختلف خریده شده. عنوان «خوب است»، گزارش «خیلی کمتر از سقف» است و دماها ثبت شده‌اند."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 25-26. Choose TWO letters, A-E.","qtype":"mcq2","questions":[{"n":25,"n2":26,"kind":"mcq2","prompt":"Which TWO parts of the course do the students say helped them most?","options":["A the laboratory safety sessions","B the statistics workshop","C the visit to a farm","D the online quizzes","E a visiting expert’s presentation"],"correct":[1,4],"evidence":"the best thing was the guest talk by the food scientist","why":{"en":"Maya: the statistics workshop; Dev agrees and adds the guest talk, which gave them the idea for the project. The safety sessions were \"repetitive\", the farm visit was cancelled, and Dev \"didn’t bother\" with the quizzes.","tr":"Maya: istatistik atölyesi; Dev katılıyor ve konuk konuşmayı ekliyor, proje fikri oradan çıkmış. Güvenlik dersleri \"tekrarlayıcı\", çiftlik ziyareti iptal edildi, Dev de testlerle \"pek uğraşmadı\".","fa":"مایا: کارگاه آمار؛ دِو موافق است و سخنرانی مهمان را هم اضافه می‌کند که ایده‌ی پروژه از آن آمد. جلسه‌های ایمنی «تکراری» بودند، بازدید مزرعه لغو شد و دِو «زیاد سراغ» آزمونک‌ها نرفت."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","PARA-opinion"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 27-30. Complete the flow-chart below. Choose FOUR answers from the box and write the correct letter, A-F, next to Questions 27-30.","qtype":"flow-chart","flowTitle":"Revising the vitamin C project","bank":["A change the final section of the report","B have the measuring equipment checked","C get all the produce from the same source","D include pictures of the samples","E carry out more trials","F replace online sources with academic ones"],"questions":[{"n":27,"kind":"match","prompt":"Step 1: ___ on the same day","correct":2,"evidence":"buy all the vegetables from a single supplier","why":{"en":"\"This time we buy all the vegetables from a single supplier, and on the same day.\" The tutor: \"that has to come first\".","tr":"\"Bu sefer bütün sebzeleri tek bir tedarikçiden ve aynı gün alacağız.\" Görevli: \"bu önce gelmeli\".","fa":"«این بار همه‌ی سبزی‌ها را از یک فروشنده و در یک روز می‌خریم». استاد: «این باید اول انجام شود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":28,"kind":"match","prompt":"Step 2: ___ (five portions for each method)","correct":4,"evidence":"increase the number of tests","why":{"en":"The technician idea is turned down (\"I don’t think that’s necessary\"). The next step is to increase the number of tests.","tr":"Teknisyen fikri reddediliyor (\"Bence gerekli değil\"). Sonraki adım test sayısını artırmak.","fa":"ایده‌ی تکنسین رد می‌شود («فکر نمی‌کنم لازم باشد»). قدم بعدی بیشتر کردن تعداد آزمایش‌هاست."},"trap":["TR-ruledout"]},{"n":29,"kind":"match","prompt":"Step 4: ___","correct":5,"evidence":"We'll use journal articles instead of the websites","why":{"en":"After the new analysis: \"We’ll use journal articles instead of the websites.\"","tr":"Yeni analizden sonra: \"Siteler yerine dergi makalelerini kullanacağız.\"","fa":"بعد از تحلیل دوباره: «به جای سایت‌ها از مقاله‌های مجله‌های علمی استفاده می‌کنیم»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":30,"kind":"match","prompt":"Step 5: ___ so that it matches the data","correct":0,"evidence":"We'll rewrite it so that it only says what the new data actually shows","why":{"en":"Photographs are rejected. \"The last step\": rewrite the conclusion.","tr":"Fotoğraflar reddediliyor. \"Son adım\": sonucu yeniden yazmak.","fa":"عکس‌ها رد می‌شوند. «قدم آخر»: بازنویسی نتیجه‌گیری."},"trap":["TR-ruledout"]}]}],"flow":{"title":"Revising the vitamin C project","steps":["Step 1: (27) ___ on the same day","Step 2: (28) ___ (five portions for each method)","Step 3: analyse the new results again, using the method from the statistics workshop","Step 4: (29) ___","Step 5: (30) ___ so that it matches the data"]},"audio":{"voices":{"Announcer":{"accent":"British (standard Southern)","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bm_george"},"role":"Recorded rubric"},"Tutor":{"accent":"British (standard Southern)","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bm_daniel"},"role":"Tutor"},"Maya":{"accent":"Scottish","gender":"F","tts":{"engine":"piper","voice":"en_GB-alba-medium"},"role":"Student"},"Dev":{"accent":"North American","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"am_adam"},"role":"Student"}},"sequence":[{"type":"announcer","text":"Part 3. You will hear a tutor talking to two students, Maya and Dev, about their project on cooking and vitamin C. First, you have some time to look at Questions 21 to 26."},{"type":"pause","seconds":30,"note":"reading time, Questions 21-26"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen carefully and answer Questions 21 to 26."},{"type":"sfx","note":"small office: a door closing at the start, quiet room tone"},{"type":"lines","from":0,"to":17},{"type":"announcer","text":"Before you hear the rest of the discussion, you have some time to look at Questions 27 to 30."},{"type":"pause","seconds":30,"note":"reading time, Questions 27-30"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen and answer Questions 27 to 30."},{"type":"lines","from":18,"to":30},{"type":"announcer","text":"That is the end of Part 3. You now have half a minute to check your answers.","after":30}]},"id":"c-x02-l3-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-l3"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"A tutor says \"Your sample size is rather small.\" This means you...","options":["wrote too few pages","used photos that were too small","tested too few examples"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"The sample size is how many things or people you tested.","tr":"Örneklem büyüklüğü, kaç şeyi ya da kişiyi test ettiğindir.","fa":"حجم نمونه یعنی چند چیز یا چند نفر را آزمایش کرده‌ای."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":3,"prompt":"\"I don’t think that’s necessary,\" says the tutor about an idea. The idea is...","options":["accepted","rejected","left until later"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"Not necessary\" = we will not do it.","tr":"\"Gerekli değil\" = onu yapmayacağız.","fa":"«لازم نیست» یعنی انجامش نمی‌دهیم."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Which words tell you that a new step in a plan has started?","options":["once you have..., after that, the last step","for example, to be honest","I agree, fair enough"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Order words move the plan forward; the others give examples or agreement.","tr":"Sıra kelimeleri planı ilerletir; diğerleri örnek ya da onay bildirir.","fa":"کلمه‌های ترتیب برنامه را جلو می‌برند؛ بقیه مثال یا موافقت را نشان می‌دهند."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Student: \"I was afraid the introduction was too short.\" Tutor: \"No, it’s the right length.\" Is \"the introduction is too short\" a problem to fix?","options":["Yes: the student says so","Only in part","No: the tutor rejects it"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"It was the student’s fear. The tutor’s \"No\" decides.","tr":"Bu öğrencinin korkusuydu. Görevlinin \"Hayır\"ı belirleyici.","fa":"این ترسِ دانشجو بود. «نه»ی استاد تعیین‌کننده است."}},{"tests":"method","point":1,"prompt":"A flow-chart has four gaps and a box of six options. How many letters do you use?","options":["all six","four, each once","four, one of them twice"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"Choose FOUR answers\": four different letters; two are left over.","tr":"\"DÖRT cevap seç\": dört farklı harf; ikisi artar.","fa":"«چهار جواب انتخاب کن»: چهار حرفِ متفاوت؛ دو تا اضافه می‌مانند."}}],"id":"c-x02-l3-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-l3"}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
